<h2>Information collected</h2>

<h3>Newsletter subscriptions</h3>
<p>If you subscribe via the newsletter form, {{ metadata.author.name }} collects your name and email address through <a href="https://loops.so/privacy" rel="noopener">Loops</a>, the email service used to send letters. Subscriptions use double opt-in — you'll get a confirmation email before you're actually added to the list.</p>

<h3>Website analytics</h3>
<p>This site uses <a href="https://umami.is/" rel="noopener">Umami</a>, a self-hosted, privacy-first analytics tool that:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Does not use cookies</li>
  <li>Does not collect personally identifying information</li>
  <li>Does not store your raw IP address — it's used only to approximate your country, then discarded</li>
  <li>Runs on a server {{ metadata.author.name }} controls directly — analytics data is never sent to a third-party analytics company</li>
</ul>
<p>Collected data includes page views, referring site, approximate location (country level), device/browser type, and — if you arrived via a tagged link — campaign source information (UTM parameters). This data is aggregate and isn't tied back to you individually.</p>

<h3>Webmentions</h3>
<p>This site accepts <a href="https://webmention.io/" rel="noopener">webmentions</a> — a way for other sites to register that they've linked to or replied to a letter. If your site sends one, the mention (your site's URL and the linked content) is displayed publicly alongside the letter it references.</p>

<h2>How this information is used</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Sending the newsletter to subscribers</li>
  <li>Understanding which letters and pages get read, to inform what gets written next</li>
  <li>Basic security and abuse prevention</li>
</ul>

<h2>Third-party services</h2>
<p>Two third-party services are involved in running this site:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Loops:</strong> newsletter delivery and subscriber management</li>
  <li><strong>Webmention.io:</strong> receiving and relaying webmentions from other sites</li>
</ul>
<p>Website analytics (Umami) are <strong>not</strong> a third-party service — they run on infrastructure {{ metadata.author.name }} operates directly. See "Website analytics" above.</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>You can:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time, via the link in any email</li>
  <li>Request a copy of the data held about you</li>
  <li>Request correction or deletion of your data</li>
</ul>
<p>To exercise any of these, email <a href="mailto:{{ metadata.author.email }}">{{ metadata.author.email }}</a>.</p>

<h2>Data retention</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Newsletter subscribers:</strong> until you unsubscribe or request deletion</li>
  <li><strong>Analytics data:</strong> retained indefinitely on the self-hosted instance unless deleted on request — since it isn't tied to an identifiable person, there's no per-person record to expire</li>
</ul>

<h2>Legal basis (GDPR)</h2>
<p>Processing is based on your consent (newsletter subscription, given via double opt-in) and legitimate interest (understanding site usage to improve the content). If you're in the EU/EEA or UK, you have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection supervisory authority.</p>

<h2>Children's privacy</h2>
<p>This site isn't directed at children under 13, and no personal information is knowingly collected from them.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>Updates will be posted on this page with a revised "Last updated" date.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:{{ metadata.author.email }}">{{ metadata.author.email }}</a>.</p>

